Panel cards: re-homed (choice (a), not a floating.rs compat shim)
- floating.rs, the legacy floating_panels model and drop targets are gone upstream, and craft-ui
  now draws the icon columns itself; a compat shim would have had to re-implement them. Cards are
  now Varos-owned (PanelStack.live: tabs, front tab, rect), drawn in the main window as before
  (not OS windows). A card's panels stay in their iconic column in the layout, so icons never
  disappear. Persisted fields keep their names (cards, places, groups) plus `live`; older ui.json
  files with only `cards` reopen those cards. open_panel still names the newest card.
- Drops: on another card's header = tabs; on a docked group's tab/drag bar = joins that group
  (Action::Move, card closes); on an icon column = closes. Dock edges come from craft-ui hit rects.
- Behaviour change: workspaces no longer carry cards (craft-ui layouts don't); a workspace switch
  keeps cards whose panels stay in an icon column (test renamed a_workspace_switch_keeps_the_cards).
  The "card holding a dock tab (Layers)" case is gone (test replaced by
  a_card_dropped_on_the_dock_joins_its_group).

Other fixes the merge needed
- crates/text/src/kashida.rs + layout.rs: upstream made every zero-length glyph its own cluster
  (list markers); a Varos virtual tatweel now stays in its letter's cluster (kashida::extends) in
  line breaking and visual order — without it tatweels were drawn on the wrong side.
- egui 0.37 port of Varos code: Id::new -> Id::unique, Ui::id -> scope_id, WidgetType -> Role,
  MouseWheel `source`, raw_input_hook(ctx, raw), capture test on the CaptureSlot pipeline, picker
  fields named for accessibility (kittest checks), home chrome test reads panel ids as egui 0.37
  makes them (scope_id + IdSalt).
- Tests adapted to the kept Varos model: upstream's kashida tests (typecmd, textimport, pdf,
  paragraph panel, tests_justify) now check the level mapping; upstream's
  justified_arabic_lines_take_their_room_on_kashidas removed (it tests the dropped upstream engine);
  install_fonts test expects the Varos faces first; docking native test makes a document first
  (Home shows no panels); docking flyout test sets keep_open=false (as before for upstream pop-out
  tests); varos-agents tests build the new Artboard fields; varos_board builds them too.

